>>
endobj
143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Today, I want to talk about the fourth dimension and what it means to me. Pastor Teresa mentioned the mission of the Joseph Business School: living independent of this world system. But what does it really mean to live by faith and not by sight? What does it mean to allow God to do the supernatural in our lives in a way that the world takes notice?)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Consider the story of David and Goliath. David recognized his spiritual authority to such a degree that he was able to slay a giant with just three smooth stones, using only one. When we think about our capacity as believers and our ability to operate in the supernatural realm, we should strive to have a revelation of who God has called us to be.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 115 0 R
/Pg 10 0 R
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (CHAPTER 3:  DISTINGUISHING GOD'S SYSTEM FROM THE WORLD SYSTEM)
/E (CHAPTER 3:  DISTINGUISHING GOD'S SYSTEM FROM THE WORLD SYSTEM)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (There is a clear delineation between the world system and God's system. As believers, we are supposed to be in the world but not of the world. However, many believers struggle to distinguish between the two. The world relies on the bank, falls into debt, and faces divorce. How can we, as the body of Christ, show the world that we are different?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Our job is to represent God on earth so that people begin to envy us and desire to be like us as we are like Christ. In corporate environments, if you don't perform, you get fired. But in the church, we often ask for more grace. Today, I challenge you not to lean on grace but to lean on faith to do the impossible.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 116 0 R
/Pg 11 0 R
>>
endobj
150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (CHAPTER 4:  EMBRACING FAITH OVER GRACE)
/E (CHAPTER 4:  EMBRACING FAITH OVER GRACE)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Grace is available, but faith is even more powerful. With faith, you can speak to mountains and they must move. You can call things that are not as though they were. Instead of asking God for more grace, ask Him to help your unbelief and increase your faith to do what He has called you to do.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 116 0 R
/Pg 11 0 R
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 117 0 R
/Pg 12 0 R
>>
endobj
154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (CHAPTER 5:  SCRIPTURAL FOUNDATIONS)
/E (CHAPTER 5:  SCRIPTURAL FOUNDATIONS)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
155 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Let's turn to a couple of scriptures. In Isaiah 11:1-2, it says, "There shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots. The spirit of the Lord shall rest upon him, the spirit of wisdom and understanding, the spirit of counsel and might, the spirit of knowledge and of the fear of the Lord.")
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
156 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (God loves rods. He uses them as symbols of authority and power. In Genesis 1:28, it says, "And God blessed them, and God said unto them, Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth, and subdue it: and have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over every living thing that moveth upon the earth.")
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 117 0 R
/Pg 12 0 R
>>
endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 118 0 R
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (CHAPTER 6:  OPERATING IN THE ANOINTING)
/E (CHAPTER 6:  OPERATING IN THE ANOINTING)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The facets of the anointing mentioned in Isaiah 11:1-2 represent the power and ability of God. When we talk about the anointing, we refer to the spirit of the Lord, wisdom, understanding, counsel, might, knowledge, and the fear of the Lord. These are the attributes that empower us to operate in the fourth-dimensional realm.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
