>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (CHAPTER 7:  THE REVELATION OF THE ANOINTING)
/E (CHAPTER 7:  THE REVELATION OF THE ANOINTING)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (When I first started working for Dr. Winston, I presented him with a corporate-style presentation. I thought I was helping the church with my corporate experience. However, Dr. Winston told me, "This is not anointed." I didn't understand what that meant. In the corporate world, I knew profit and loss, but the concept of "anointed" was foreign to me. Dr. Winston explained that the anointing removes burdens and destroys yokes, and my presentation felt burdensome.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The anointing of God, when it rests upon you, grants wisdom that no one can resist. The Bible says if you lack wisdom, you can ask God, and He will give it liberally. This includes the spirit of counsel and might. If you don't know which way to go, you can ask God for counsel.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
