169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (CHAPTER 8:  REAL-LIFE APPLICATION OF THE ANOINTING)
/E (CHAPTER 8:  REAL-LIFE APPLICATION OF THE ANOINTING)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Dr. Winston once faced a challenge with the property for his church. He had purchased a mall, but the municipality refused to allow church services in the building. Dr. Winston prayed, and God instructed him to read the scripture to the mayor. Despite not having an appointment, he pressed forth with faith and boldness.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (How many of us would go to the bank with a Bible because God told us to? It may sound good in theory, but living it out is different. Dr. Winston, a black man, went to a white mayor who had already denied his request. But through obedience and faith, the mayor allowed church services, demonstrating the power of living apart from the world system.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
