/E (CHAPTER 10:  THE FEAR OF THE LORD)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The spirit of knowledge and the fear of the Lord are crucial components of the anointing. The fear of the Lord is not about trembling in terror, but about profound reverence. When God shows up, everything changes. The fear of the Lord means understanding the extent of His power and giving Him the reverence He deserves.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (To operate in the fourth-dimensional realm, you must leave your flesh. Although we are spirit beings, we often operate in the flesh, limiting our potential. If you only see yourself as flesh, you miss out on the spiritual authority God has given you. Gideon, for example, saw himself as insignificant, but God saw a mighty man of valor. When you see yourself as God sees you, you can accomplish the impossible.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
